<title>SWEDEN: Volvo sees Japan sales up 4 pct in '97.</title>
<headline>Volvo sees Japan sales up 4 pct in '97.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish vehicle maker AB Volvo said on Thursday it planned to sell 25,000 cars in Japan in 1997, or four percent more than in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;We will sell at least 25,000 cars in Japan this year,&quot; Volvo Cars spokesman Ulf Thorne told Reuters.</p>
<p>Sales in Japan rose 17 percent in 1996 compared with a year earlier.</p>
<p>&quot;The goal for the year is a realistic estimate which is done in Japan and takes into account our model range and how we estimate the market will develop this year,&quot; Thorne said.</p>
<p>-- Henrik Alberius, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1250</p>
</text>
